a6e14899ec00436781655501f3ba3586d1418dce1f34331e1a", "types/fq_default_poly.cp313-win_amd64.pyd": "d4d02738f5946769a0e0fdc69ddfa72fb0e12ddd1d12b90d015d408703093faa", "types/nmod.cp313-win_amd64.pyd": "9c54eee5ff195f370b0d6e566686deb16700c2f30ff8e0452ae6b6393edd7ea5", "types/nmod_mat.cp313-win_amd64.pyd": "1b952ba75ceb987ab0e2f15261d53df4124797aba8c7552ced5f0c5e3b45add4", "types/nmod_mpoly.cp313-win_amd64.pyd": "e3d39c8178ad7e436c650074daa37b0c7f1be7178cb7bdaab4b2b611690b6ff5", "types/nmod_poly.cp313-win_amd64.pyd": "7c91ad8a544e31b566aae8c79f2493ec19bc01d3b0f87ed242ef30daa378e423", "types/nmod_series.cp313-win_amd64.pyd": "de6748c4a209dc1f7dbdcc16269c4566e6f323aaba0d6dbd5cd495516feae3b8", "typing.py": "a9e5aaaa561599f76931bcc947cfc8cbe3e8da528692482e7db12d98397b81e2", "utils/__init__.py": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855", "utils/flint_exceptions.py": "88bd68c2d4b41a2d18c48a5e80906278a96bf47252620b65671bd3c66d466362"}}, "frozen_sources_utf8": {"notes/current-coupled-input-energy-bound.md": "# Complete fixed-seed input-energy conversion; coupled strong test remains open\n\n2026-10-25 HST, E003/S169. Ordinary argument before frozen verification.\nPrevious goal turn: no progress. Full stable-wormhole objective incomplete.\nThe closed feasibility audit and original physical targets are preserved.\n\nThis addresses the energy input factors in the complete return error, not\nthe missing strong output map. All quantum terms enter through the actual\ntwo-sided finite-seed comparison. No physical Hessian application or signed\ncoupled solve is claimed. The requested quantitative feasibility milestone\nremains incomplete.\n\n## 1. Exact global inverse of the frozen York conversion\n\nUse the current finite polynomial Q, exact positive-temperature root z_h,\nand the original paired mass/log phase. In the notation of\ncurrent-physical-york-dual-assembly.md set X=QJ=z^2 y and\nA=Q''-4Q'/z. Its two kinematic equations give exactly\n\n    -y''+[6/z^2+2A/(3Q)]y=2T'/(3z^2)-8T/(3z^3),\n    y(0)=y(z_h)=0,\n    xi=-T-z y-z^2 y'/2,\n    s=nu+T/2+z^2 y'/4-z y/2.                         (1)\n\nThese endpoint conditions express the original outer-fixed return and\nfinite J at the regular bolt. They are not new physical boundary data.\nThe potential's 1/(z_h-z) singularity has the regular solution y=O(z_h-z);\nthen J=z^2y/Q is finite. On the mass/log core y=O(z^2 log^k z) at zero.\nAt the bolt a smooth stationary T yields the regular one-sided solution\nby substitution in (1). Completion uses this variational realization.\n\nLet P=6/z^2+2A/(3Q). On the WHOLE physical interval P>=5/z^2.\nIndeed Q+(2/3)z^2 A equals\n\n    beta-3u z^2+3a z^3-(5/3)b4 z^4-2eps z^5+5eps z^6,\n\nwhere a=4beta+2u+tau and b4=3beta+u+eps. It is bounded below by\nbeta-3u-5|eps|>0 since 3a-5b4/3>0. Keep Q>0 only on the actual interval;\nno division by a separately rounded bolt value is performed.\n\nPut l=1-log z and\n\n    N(f)=||sqrt(l) f/z^2||2+||sqrt(l) f'/z||2\n         +||sqrt(l) f''||2+||sqrt(l) Q^(3/2) f'''||2,          (2)\n\nwith measure dz on (0,z_h). This is an explicitly specified INPUT norm,\nnot a redefinition of the physical admission norm or fast output.\nTesting (1) with l y and integrating before bounding gives\n\n    E_y=int [l y'^2+(l P-1/(2z^2))y^2],\n    E_y>=||sqrt(l)y'||2^2+(9/2)||sqrt(l)y/z||2^2,\n    sqrt(E_y)<=c ||sqrt(l)T/z^2||2, c=2sqrt(17)/9.     (3)\n\nThe right pairing is -(2/3)int l(T/z^2)[y'+(2-1/l)y/z].\nCauchy--Schwarz in the two energy components proves (3). Truncation and\nthe displayed endpoint rates justify the logarithmic test; no unproved\nboundary term is dropped.\n\nAn important cancellation occurs in the physical scalar Laplacian. Define\nL_s=Qs''+(Q'-2Q/z)s'. Direct substitution, BEFORE division by Q, gives\n\n    L_s=L_nu+(QT')'/3+(2Q'/(3z)-2Q/z^2)T\n       +(Q+z^2Q''/6-2zQ'/3)y'\n       +(z^3Q'''/6-2z^2Q''/3+5zQ'/3-2Q)y/z.          (4)\n\nThere is no inverse Q in these coefficients. The actual seed has\n|Q|<.17, |Q'|<.3, |Q''|<2.1, |Q'''|<8.1 and |A|<3.\nAlso (A/Q)_-<1e-9: for z>=1e-9 use\nA>=z(6a-4b4)-6u-6|eps|>0; below it Q>.16.\nEquations (3)-(4) and\n\n    s'=nu'+T'/3+2T/(3z)+(A/(6Q)+1/z^2)z^2y\n\ntherefore give, with N=N(nu)+N(T),\n\n    ||sqrt(l)s/z^2||2<N,\n    ||sqrt(l Q)s'/z||2<N,\n    ||sqrt(l)L_s||2<3N,  ||sqrt(l)(Qs')'||2<4N.       (5)\n\nFor the apparent gradient denominator, keep the potential energy:\nint l |A|y^2/Q <=(1.5+2e-9/(9/2)) E_y. Thus its contribution is at most\n[sqrt(3(1.5+2e-9/(9/2)))/6+sqrt(.17/(9/2))]sqrt(E_y).\nThe remaining T/z^2 coefficient is 2sqrt(.17)/3; their sum is <1.\nFor (4) the corresponding coefficient is\n.54+.72c+3.59c/sqrt(9/2)<3. These are global bounds, not cold asymptotics.\n\nThe TT scalar return S=nu-s depends only on T. The same bounds hold for\nS with N(T), by setting nu=0 and reversing the sign. In particular BOTH\ndiagonal form inputs are controlled; no indefinite total-action bound\nis incorrectly substituted for their positive sum.\n\n## 2. Complete action-energy bound in the original units\n\nUse the exact local generator in current-finite-local-action-assembly.md\nand the same affine chart/frozen York congruence. Normalize N=1 temporarily\nby homogeneity, not by changing an admission target. For EACH of (s,0)\nand (S,T), (5) permits the following integral product majorants:\n\n    nu0<=1, T0<=1, gradient<=1, L_nu<=3, Delta nu<=4,\n    Delta T<=1, D0*z^2<=6, |delta D|_L2(l dz)<=20,\n    integral |delta^2 D|/z^2<=12.\n\nIn the Weyl polynomial use seed/first/second majorants\nphi=(1,1,0), L=(3,2,0), M=(1,4,0), Nphi=(1,1,2).\nThe seed phi entry represents |log z|<=l, not a uniform bound by one.\nSeed M,Nphi,D carry z^-2; variation nu and T carry the compensating z^2\nin (2). All second products are bounded by weighted L2 Cauchy--Schwarz.\nThere is at most one undifferentiated phi, so the single l weight suffices.\nExponential jets are (1,|k|,k^2). Multiplying these triples gives a\nreproducible positive upper bound for every term of the exact generator.\n\nRetain the shared trial vacuum interval, actual a2, exact LLL and complete\npositive geodesic term. Its full sixth-moment bound is\n\n    Pgeo/|W| <= [2/(525pi B^2)] [4C^2/q_flux] Z,\n    Z=int Q[(5/8)Q^2 T'''^2+(3/2)Q T''' U+U^2]dz,\n    U=(3/2)Q'T''+(1/2)Q''T',   Z<2 N(T)^2.          (6)\n\nThis includes the whole angular spectrum and every flow frequency. The\nactual thermal, paired-boundary, coincidence and finite-domain differences\nremain in |l-l0|<=.0022 l. The scalar diagonal is unchanged by that\ncomparison. No determinant is replaced by a finite list of angular modes.\nThe complete normalized comparison diagonal majorant is <78.000004;\nusing it for both diagonals gives\n\n    [a(s)+l(xi)]/|W| < 2(78.000004) N^2/(1-.0022).\n\nRestore the original radial energy, removing the SAME factor 4pi beta_T\nper half from the action, beta_T=2pi B/(C gamma). Since\n|W|/(N_halves 4pi beta_T)=CB/(8piG), the exact conversion is\n\n    E(u)^2=[a(s)+l(xi)]/(|W| beta),\n    E(u)<31 [N(nu)+N(T)].                            (7)\n\nThe evaluated upper expression is near 30.627827. This is an INPUT-to-\nenergy bound at the seed. It is not energy-to-graph, R_X, or an X-ball\nestimate. The inverse direction is not asserted.\n\n## 3. Exact contribution to complete-return errors\n\nFor R_s and H_s of current-short-travel-strong-domain.md, keep\neta_s=.0022000000000000032 and q_s=eta_s/(1-eta_s). Equations (7) and\nthe ACTUAL coupled inverse prove for EVERY input in (2), independently\nof whether it is fast, a boundary phase or interior,\n\n    E(H^-1 R_s v)<=31 eta_s N(v),\n    E(H_s^-1 R_s v)<=31 q_s N(v).                    (8)\n\nThus for an actual source column F_j=R_s Phi_j its input factor in\nthe complete tail is U_j<=31 eta_s N(Phi_j), and\n\n    error_ij<=M_i,p q_s^(Niter-p) 31 eta_s N(Phi_j).   (9)\n\nThis closes a numerical conversion for the FULL coupled energy response\nto these specified columns, including scalar/TT mixing. It does not set\nan unspecified post-elimination F_j equal to R_s Phi_j. Additional source\nmaps in the original global matching system still need their own norms.\nNor does (8) compute a signed output, M_i,p, or the graph feedback norm.\n\nFor the retained Niter=64, p=4 graph-tail allocation, a sufficient\nrounded-down replacement for M_graph,4 U_feedback<=1.5062e156 is\n\n    M_graph,4 N_feedback<=2.2085e157,                 (10)\n\nONLY when the complete feedback source under consideration is R_s times\nan input map with the stated N_feedback norm. Use the upward guard\n31 eta_s<.0682000000001 in this substitution. Neither N_feedback nor\nM_graph,4 is assigned one. The original matching system may contain\nadditional input maps, so (10) is not a certificate for its full feedback.\nThe sharper established affine energy bound 1.1e-10 is unchanged.\n\nThe exact mass lift, its arbitrary previously fixed cutoff transition,\nscalar quartic and exact correlated slow pair all belong to (2). Their\nactual cutoff derivative norms must be inserted before quoting individual\nnumerical U_j; no unspecified smooth cutoff is assigned convenient jets.\nFor the correlated pair its jets must be evaluated using B0 e_* and\nexpm1, as in operators/exact_slow_phase.py, rather than separate B0 terms.\nThe present acceptance evaluates the universal constant (7)-(8), not those\nindividual column norms. This limitation is explicit.\n\n## 4. Unresolved feasibility decision\n\nThe first missing STRONG argument remains numerical bounds for the complete\ndifferentiated R_s kernel and contacts, composed with the actual inverse,\noriginal phase/moment equations and finite-domain reconstruction. The\nknown H3->L2 interior estimate supplies no differentiated output constant.\nNo external smooth-boundary theorem is imported to fill that gap.\n\nNo kappa_m, signed coupled center, actual mass or complete feedback norm\nwas computed. At conditional kappa_m=5e-5, the remaining affine and graph\nbudgets are still 5.34235e-12 and .0012069, with the independent energy\ndebit .0195239. The conversion >.00906808164|m| in the ORIGINAL fast norm\nis unchanged. The screen .135973<.1599164 retains its two-fast-input\nadmitted-family scope; (8) gives independent phase control only in energy.\nNo nonlinear neighborhood follows from these seed statements.\n\nRESEARCH DECISION: retain the construction and the complete strong-return\nmethod. Use (7)-(9) for its actual input-energy costs; do not insert them\nfor the missing strong output constants. The kinematic conversion does\nnot force a tiny-bolt denominator loss. Quantitative feasibility remains\nundecided, with no construction obstruction established.\n\nONE NEXT CALCULATION (PROPOSED, NOT EXECUTED): bound the complete original-\noutput composition T_old(H_s^-1 R_s)^4, including common-restored contacts,\nall angular/thermal contributions and original matching/bolt returns.\nCombine its bound with (9) only for the identified source columns; the\nremaining matching input maps and signed solve are still required.\n\nRemaining to-do list: complete strong return and signed coupled response;\noriginal physical-norm comparisons; nonlinear admission/contraction and\nexact compatibility; physical matching; semiclassical validity/noise;\nall-sector stability and the full stable semiclassical wormhole objective.\n", "checks/current_coupled_input_energy_bound.py": "\"\"\"Universal complete seed input-energy bound; not a strong coupled solve.\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom math import comb\nimport json, sys, traceback\nimport sympy as sp\nif '--arb-path' in sys.argv:\n    sys.path.insert(0, sys.argv[sys.argv.index('--arb-path')+1])\nimport flint\nfrom flint import arb, ctx\nctx.prec=512\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nSTEM='current-coupled-input-energy-bound'\nOWN=['notes/'+STEM+'.md','checks/current_coupled_input_energy_bound.py',\n     'evidence/'+STEM+'-review.json']\nsys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'checks'))\nsaved_argv=sys.argv[:]\nsys.argv=[sys.argv[0]]\nimport current_physical_york_dual_assembly as york\nsys.argv=saved_argv\nCHECKS=[]\ndef check(name,value,detail=None):\n    CHECKS.append(dict(name=name,passed=bool(value)))\n    if not value: raise AssertionError(name)\nyork.check=check\nyork.prior.check=check\ndef enc(v):\n    m,r,e=v.mid_rad_10exp(60)\n    return dict(ball=v.str(40),decimal_enclosure=dict(mid=str(m),rad=str(r),exponent=str(e)))\n\nclass Jet:\n    \"\"\"Positive integral product majorants justified in the ordinary argument.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self,v=0,d=0,dd=0): self.v,self.d,self.dd=map(arb,(v,d,dd))\n    @staticmethod\n    def lift(x):return x if isinstance(x,Jet) else Jet(x)\n    def __add__(self,x):\n        x=self.lift(x);return Jet(self.v+x.v,self.d+x.d,self.dd+x.dd)\n    __radd__=__add__\n    def __mul__(self,x):\n        x=self.lift(x)\n        return Jet(self.v*x.v,self.d*x.v+self.v*x.d,self.dd*x.v+2*self.d*x.d+self.v*x.dd)\n    __rmul__=__mul__\n    def __truediv__(self,x):return self*(1/arb(x))\n    def __pow__(self,k):\n        out=Jet(1)\n        for _ in range(k):out=out*self\n        return out\n\ndef execute():\n    z=sp.symbols('z',positive=True)\n    Q=sp.Function('Q')(z);X=sp.Function('X')(z)\n    T=sp.Function('T')(z);nu=sp.Function('nu')(z)\n    A=sp.diff(Q,z,2)-4*sp.diff(Q,z)/z\n    x2=4*sp.diff(X,z)/z+sp.Rational(2,3)*A*X/Q-sp.Rational(2,3)*sp.diff(T,z)+sp.Rational(8,3)*T/z\n    J=X/Q;xi=-T-sp.diff(X,z)/2\n    residual=-sp.diff(Q**2/z**4*sp.diff(J,z),z)-Q/z**4*(4*xi/z-sp.diff(xi,z))\n    check('exact_inverse_York_equation',sp.simplify(residual.subs(sp.diff(X,z,2),x2))==0)\n    scalar=nu+T/2+sp.diff(X,z)/4-X/z\n    lap=Q*sp.diff(scalar,z,2)+(sp.diff(Q,z)-2*Q/z)*sp.diff(scalar,z)\n    lap=lap.subs(sp.diff(X,z,3),sp.diff(x2,z)).subs(sp.diff(X,z,2),x2)\n    y=sp.Function('y')(z)\n    lap=lap.subs({sp.diff(X,z):2*z*y+z*z*sp.diff(y,z),X:z*z*y})\n    by=Q+z*z*sp.diff(Q,z,2)/6-2*z*sp.diff(Q,z)/3\n    cy=z**3*sp.diff(Q,z,3)/6-2*z*z*sp.diff(Q,z,2)/3+5*z*sp.diff(Q,z)/3-2*Q\n    expected=Q*sp.diff(nu,z,2)+(sp.diff(Q,z)-2*Q/z)*sp.diff(nu,z)+sp.diff(Q*sp.diff(T,z),z)/3+(2*sp.diff(Q,z)/(3*z)-2*Q/z**2)*T+by*sp.diff(y,z)+cy*y/z\n    check('exact_laplacian_cancellation_no_inverse_Q',sp.simplify(lap-expected)==0)\n    p,h,zh,env=york.actual_parameters()\n    coeff={k:env[v] for k,v in zip(york.powers,york.qs)}\n    beta,u,eps=coeff[0],coeff[2],coeff[6]\n    aa,b4=-coeff[3],coeff[4]\n    check('potential_coercivity_whole_interval',beta-3*u-5*abs(eps)>0 and 3*aa-5*b4/3>0)\n    # Exact Bernstein range over [0,1], including the physical [0,z_h].\n    def polynomial_derivative(c):return {k-1:k*v for k,v in c.items() if k}\n    def bernstein(c):\n        n=max(c)\n        return [sum((c.get(i,arb(0))*arb(comb(k,i))/comb(n,i) for i in range(k+1)),arb(0)) for k in range(n+1)]\n    q1=polynomial_derivative(coeff);q2=polynomial_derivative(q1);q3=polynomial_derivative(q2)\n    ac={k-2:k*(k-5)*v for k,v in coeff.items() if k>=2}\n    check('global_Q_guard',all(abs(v)<arb('.17') for v in bernstein(coeff)))\n    check('global_Qprime_guard',12*beta*arb(4)/27+u/2+6*abs(eps)+3*p['tau']<arb('.3'))\n    check('global_Qsecond_guard',all(abs(v)<arb('2.1') for v in bernstein(q2)))\n    check('global_Qthird_guard',all(abs(v)<arb('8.1') for v in bernstein(q3)))\n    check('global_A_guard',all(abs(v)<3 for v in bernstein(ac)))\n    zc=arb('1e-9')\n    qlo=beta-sum((abs(v)*zc**k for k,v in coeff.items() if k),arb(0))\n    check('negative_potential_part_guard',qlo>arb('.16') and (6*u+6*abs(eps))/qlo<arb('1e-9') and zc*(6*aa-4*b4)-6*u-6*abs(eps)>0)\n    c=2*arb(17).sqrt()/9\n    s0=arb('.5')+c/4+c/(2*(arb(9)/2).sqrt())\n    grad=(2*arb('.17').sqrt()/3+c*((3*(arb('1.5')+arb('2e-9')/(arb(9)/2))).sqrt()/6+(arb('.17')/(arb(9)/2)).sqrt()))\n    lap0=arb('.54')+arb('.72')*c+arb('3.59')*c/(arb(9)/2).sqrt()\n    check('weighted_value_gradient_laplacian_guards',s0<1 and grad<1 and lap0<3 and 3+2*arb('.17').sqrt()<4)\n    check('complete_sixth_moment_Z_guard',arb(5)/8+arb('1.5')*arb('.3825').sqrt()+arb('.3825')<2)\n    C,B2,q=p['C'],p['B2'],arb(p['q'])\n    phi,L,MM,NN,DD=Jet(1,1),Jet(3,2),Jet(1,4),Jet(1,1,2),Jet(6,20,12)\n    exponent=lambda k:Jet(1,abs(k),k*k)\n    en2,en4,eu2,em2=map(exponent,(2,4,2,-2))\n    la0=arb(2000)**-10\n    parts={\n      'Einstein':(en2*DD/2+en2*eu2/C+3*la0*B2/C*en4*eu2).dd,\n      'magnetic':(arb.pi()*q*q*arb(2000)**8/(C*B2)*eu2).dd,\n      'R2':(8*arb.pi()*arb('1e22')/(C*B2)*(4*eu2+4*C*DD+C*C*em2*DD**2)).dd,\n      'Weyl':((C*C*em2*(phi*L**2/60+L*MM/30+MM**2/10+L*NN/30+7*MM*NN/90+7*NN**2/180)+C*phi*L/18+(arb(1)/15+q*q/3)*phi*eu2+C*NN/18)/(2*arb.pi()*C*B2)).dd,\n      'vacuum_interval':2*(604*q*q+(1+arb('6e-9'))*(q*q/6-arb(1)/30))/(arb.pi()*C*B2),\n      'a2':100*C/(480*arb.pi()*B2)*(4*arb('2.1')**2+16*arb('2.1')+8),\n      'LLL':q*arb('.17')/(6*arb.pi()*B2),\n      'complete_positive_geodesic':2*(4*C*C/q)*2/(525*arb.pi()*B2)}\n    upper=sum(parts.values(),arb(0))\n    conversion=(2*upper/(beta*(1-arb('.0022')))).sqrt()\n    check('complete_comparison_diagonal_guard',upper<arb('78.000004'))\n    check('original_energy_input_constant',conversion<31)\n    B,G,gamma,NH,lam,Cs=sp.symbols('B G gamma NH lam C',positive=True)\n    W=NH*sp.pi*B**2/(G*gamma);period=2*sp.pi*B/(Cs*gamma)\n    check('original_action_to_radial_energy_units',sp.simplify(8*sp.pi*G/(lam*B**3)*W/(NH*4*sp.pi*period)-Cs/(lam*B**2))==0)\n    eta=arb('.0022000000000000032');qs=eta/(1-eta)\n    check('actual_Rs_input_conversion_upward_guard',31*eta<arb('.0682000000001'))\n    check('conditional_graph_tail_product_allowance',arb('2.2085e157')*arb('.0682000000001')<arb('1.5062e156'))\n    return dict(outcome='complete_strong_coupled_estimate_unresolved',\n      normalized_component_upper_bounds={k:enc(v) for k,v in parts.items()},\n      normalized_single_diagonal_upper=enc(upper),original_energy_conversion_upper_expression=enc(conversion),\n      original_energy_conversion_guard='31',weighted_York_value=enc(s0),weighted_York_gradient=enc(grad),weighted_York_Laplacian=enc(lap0),\n      complete_H_inverse_Rs_energy_per_N=enc(31*eta),complete_Hs_inverse_Rs_energy_per_N=enc(31*qs),\n      conditional_Mgraph_times_Nfeedback_allowance='2.2085e157; only for source map R_s times the specified N input',\n      norm_definition='N(nu)+N(T), weighted value/first/second and Q^(3/2) third derivatives; see ordinary argument',\n      independent_phase_energy_scope=True,individual_cutoff_column_norms_evaluated=False,\n      physical_operator_applications=0,coupled_signed_solve_executed=False,\n      complete_strong_estimate_executed=False,actual_mass=None,kappa_mass=None,\n      M_graph_4=None,M_X_8=None,U_original_matching_feedback=None,\n      original_physical_X_comparisons=False,nonlinear_neighborhood_transfer=False,\n      new_nonlinear_feasibility_gate_closed=False,nonlinear_admission=False,\n      nonlinear_contraction=False,exact_compatibility=False,physical_matching=False,\n      validity_noise=False,all_sector_stability=False,actual_controlled_solution=False,\n      construction_obstruction=False,closed_audit_preserved=True,\n      complete_angular_thermal_contacts_boundary_returns_retained=True)\n\nif __name__=='__main__':\n    mode='acceptance' if '--acceptance' in sys.argv else 'development'\n    out=ROOT/'evidence'/(STEM+('' if mode=='acceptance' else '-development')+'.json')\n    review=json.loads((ROOT/OWN[2]).read_bytes())\n    paths=set(OWN+review['retained_inputs'])\n    for module in list(sys.modules.values()):\n        f=getattr(module,'__file__',None)\n        if f:\n            try:rel=Path(f).resolve().relative_to(ROOT).as_posix()\n            except ValueError:continue\n            if rel.endswith('.py'):paths.add(rel)\n    digest=lambda p:sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    before={p:digest(ROOT/p) for p in sorted(paths)}\n    fr=Path(flint.__file__).resolve().parent\n    runtime=dict(python=sys.version,python_executable_sha256=digest(Path(sys.executable)),flint_version=flint.__version__,\n      flint_artifacts={p.relative_to(fr).as_posix():digest(p) for p in sorted(fr.rglob('*')) if p.is_file() and p.suffix in ['.py','.pyd','.dll']})\n    run=dict(started_utc=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),mode=mode,input_sha256_before=before,precision_bits=512,runtime=runtime,\n      frozen_sources_utf8={p:(ROOT/p).read_text(encoding='utf-8') for p in OWN})\n    try:\n        check('ordinary_argument_frozen',before[OWN[0]]==review['ordinary_argument_sha256'])\n        run['result']=execute()\n        run['input_sha256_after']={p:digest(ROOT/p) for p in before}\n        check('frozen_inputs_unchanged',before==run['input_sha256_after'])\n        run['status']='passed'\n    except Exception:run['status']='failed';run['traceback']=traceback.format_exc()\n    run['checks']=CHECKS;run['finished_utc']=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n    ledger=json.loads(out.read_bytes()) if out.exists() else {'runs':[]}\n    ledger['runs'].append(run);out.write_bytes((json.dumps(ledger,indent=2)+'\\n').encode())\n    with (ROOT/'evidence'/(STEM+'.log')).open('ab') as f:f.write((json.dumps(run)+'\\n').encode())\n    print(json.dumps(dict(mode=mode,status=run['status'],checks=len(CHECKS),result=run.get('result'),traceback=run.get('traceback')),indent=2))\n    if run['status']!='passed':raise SystemExit(1)\n", "evidence/current-coupled-input-energy-bound-review.json": "{\n  \"ordinary_argument_sha256\": \"99cb07232f99e39c6a4b309fe1dcd764a44c8c70b1846b9ad7e21c2b5ed9c422\",\n  \"retained_inputs\": [\n    \"notes/current-physical-york-dual-assembly.md\",\n    \"notes/current-finite-local-action-assembly.md\",\n    \"notes/current-localized-bolt-adjoint-sensitivity.md\",\n    \"notes/current-geodesic-two-sided-remainder.md\",\n    \"notes/current-global-return-energy-attempt.md\",\n    \"notes/current-short-travel-strong-domain.md\",\n    \"notes/current-coupled-return-tail-at